    "title": "Man accused of leading state troopers on chase in stolen ambulance in Beaver County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WPXI.com News Staff ,\n36 minutes ago A man is accused of stealing an ambulance and using it to flee from police in Beaver County. By MattGush A man is accused of stealing an ambulance and using it to flee from police in Beaver County.\nPennsylvania State Police said Justin R. Corrie, 23, stole an ambulance in Industry Borough at 7:57 p.m. on Wednesday.\nWhen troopers tried to pull him over, he took off in the emergency vehicle, troopers said.\nThe chase ended when police used a “legal intervention” to stop the vehicle on State Route 18 in Center Township.\nCorrie was taken into custody and is being charged with fleeing or attempting to elude police, theft of a motor vehicle, unauthorized use of a motor vehicle, reckless driving, careless driving, speeding, and other traffic violations.\nDownload the FREE WPXI News app for breaking news alerts.\nFollow Channel 11 News on Facebook and Twitter . | Watch WPXI NOW",
    "summary": "By WPXI.com News Staff , 36 minutes ago A man is accused of stealing an ambulance and using it to flee from police in Beaver County. By MattGush A man is accused of stealing an ambulance and using it to flee from police in Beaver County. Pennsylvania State Police said Justin R. Corrie, 23, stole an ambulance in Industry Borough at 7:57 p.m. on Wednesday. The chase ended when police used a “legal intervention” to stop the vehicle on State Route 18 in Center Township.",
